---
import BaseLayoutV2 from '../layouts/BaseLayoutV2.astro';
import ProductDemo from '../components/ProductDemo.astro';
import PlanComparison from '../components/PlanComparison.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
import FreeHandoff from '../components/FreeHandoff.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
import { briefStructure, freeQuestions, method, offer } from '../data/offer';
import { briefExcerpt } from '../data/brief-excerpt';
import { dates } from '../lib/benchmark';

const d = dates();
const free = offer.free;
const accountable = [
  { who: 'You', does: 'Own the decision, supply the facts and the constraints, and decide. Frame Free does not recommend at all; where you cannot answer a question, the handoff records an unknown rather than a guess.' },
  { who: 'The model', does: 'Reads, asks and drafts at speed. It does not know which fact matters to your organisation until you tell it, and it can drift from the instructions it was given.' },
  { who: 'Frame', does: 'Gives the model a process to follow: ask first, one question at a time, and tag every material claim. It is an instruction the model follows, not a guarantee of its behaviour, and it is the discipline, not the judgement.' },
  { who: 'GreenSquare AI', does: 'Writes and maintains the guide, publishes what it has and has not been shown to do, and answers for both. It does not see your decision or your data.' },
];
---
<BaseLayoutV2
  title="Frame | The Decision Brief and the method that produces it"
  description="Frame is a method for ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini. Frame Free, the beta available now, is a six-page PDF that makes the model interrogate a consequential decision and stop before evaluation."
  current="product"
>
  <section class="v-hero product-hero">
    <div class="v-container">
      <h1>Frame makes an AI interrogate the decision before it advises.</h1>
      <p class="v-lead">Frame Free is available now: a six-page PDF whose six questions clarify, inspect and test one decision, then hand back a seven-part frame. Frame Pro is in development and will continue into comparison, recommendation and a Decision Brief.</p>
      <div class="v-actions">
        <a class="v-btn v-btn--green" href="#get-free">Get Frame Free PDF</a>
        <a class="v-btn" href="#free">See the Frame Free output</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="plans">
    <div class="v-container">
      <div class="product-plans__head">
        <h2>What exists now, and what does not.</h2>
        <p>The two plans have different outputs. The boundary is shown before the demonstration so the example cannot be mistaken for the Frame Free deliverable.</p>
      </div>
      <PlanComparison />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="free">
    <div class="v-container">
      <div class="v-cols product-free">
        <div class="v-cols__head">
          <h2>Today: six questions and a seven-part handoff.</h2>
          <p>Frame Free asks six questions, one at a time. Together they cover Clarify, Inspect and Test, the first three of the method’s six steps listed further down. The six questions are not the six steps: Frame Free stops before Compare, Decide and Execute.</p>
          <a class="v-link" href={withBase('/free/')}>What Frame Free includes</a>
        </div>
        <ol class="d-list d-list--indexed">
          {freeQuestions.map(([name, q], i) => (
            <li><span class="d-list__index">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><div><h3>{name}</h3><p>{q}</p></div></li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="product-free__handoff">
        <FreeHandoff id="product-handoff" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section" id="brief">
    <div class="v-container">
      <div class="product-head">
        <h2>One decision, read in three states.</h2>
        <p>The Decision Brief is what the full method produces, and what Frame Pro is planned to produce. Frame Free does not produce one. This is the demonstration run published in the site repository: a fictional 42-branch systems cutover, run once on {briefExcerpt.provenance.model} with the method file that predates Frame, unedited. Move through the question as it was brought, one turn of interrogation, and the brief.</p>
      </div>
      <ProductDemo />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="method">
    <div class="v-container v-cols">
      <div class="v-cols__head">
        <h2>The full method: six steps.</h2>
        <p>The sequence is fixed. Frame Free’s six questions cover the first three steps and stop before evaluation; Compare, Decide and Execute belong to Frame Pro, which is in development. What the model asks inside each step depends on what you have already told it, so two decisions rarely produce the same questions.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="d-list d-list--indexed">
        {method.map(([name, text, plan], i) => (
          <li><span class="d-list__index">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><div><h3>{name}</h3><p>{text}</p><p class="method-plan">{plan === 'free' ? 'Frame Free' : 'Frame Pro, in development'}</p></div></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="receive">
    <div class="v-container v-cols">
      <div class="v-cols__head">
        <h2>One file, ready on the page.</h2>
        <p>Frame Free is the PDF and nothing else: no application, no account with us and no upload of your material to GreenSquare AI.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="product-receive">
        <dl class="d-meta">
          <div><dt>The file</dt><dd>{free.delivery.object} {free.delivery.how}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Delivery</dt><dd>{free.delivery.after}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Time</dt><dd>{free.delivery.setup} {free.session}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Compatibility</dt><dd>{free.compatibility.tested} {free.compatibility.boundary}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Your rights</dt><dd>{free.rights}</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="d-panel product-structure">
          <div class="d-panel__head"><strong>Decision Brief</strong><span>structure, the Frame Pro output</span></div>
          <ol class="product-structure__list">
            {briefStructure.map((row, i) => (
              <li><span class="d-list__index">{i + 1}</span><div><h3>{row.section}</h3><p>{row.carries}</p></div></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <div class="d-panel__foot"><p>Every material claim in the brief is tagged given, derived, inferred or unknown. The brief closes with a confidence statement and what to validate first.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="accountable">
    <div class="v-container v-cols">
      <div class="v-cols__head">
        <h2>Who remains accountable.</h2>
        <p>Four parties touch a decision run through Frame. The output is only as good as the division of labour between them, so it is stated here rather than in the terms.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="d-meta product-accountable">
        {accountable.map((row) => (
          <div><dt>{row.who}</dt><dd>{row.does}</dd></div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="evidence">
    <div class="v-container v-cols">
      <div class="v-cols__head">
        <h2>Where the evidence stops.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="d-panel product-evidence">
        <dl class="d-meta">
          <div><dt>Shown</dt><dd>In a preregistered benchmark, an earlier method file made the model ask before answering, compare real options and tag its evidence on every run. That is a change in process, and it held across two models and three cases.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Not shown</dt><dd>That the brief is better judged than one a well-briefed model produces unaided. On the three judgement checks the informed baseline matched or exceeded the loaded method.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Boundary</dt><dd>The file tested predates Frame. Nothing on this page claims the benchmark result for Frame Free or Frame Pro. Record current as at {d.currentAsAt}.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="d-panel__foot"><p><a href={withBase('/research/')}>Research overview</a>, <a href={withBase('/benchmark/')}>benchmark record</a> and <a href={withBase('/methodology/')}>methodology</a>.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="pro">
    <div class="v-container v-cols">
      <div class="v-cols__head">
        <h2>Frame Pro</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="d-panel product-pro">
        <div class="d-panel__head"><strong>{offer.pro.name}</strong><span>{offer.pro.status}</span></div>
        <div class="d-panel__body"><p class="v-small">{offer.pro.note} Until then the Frame Free beta is the only plan, and it is the one this page describes.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Signup location="product_footer" />
</BaseLayoutV2>

<style>
  .product-hero h1 { max-width: 20ch; }
  .product-hero .v-lead { max-width: 60ch; }
  .product-plans__head { max-width: 62ch; margin-bottom: var(--v-6); }
  .product-plans__head p { color: var(--v-ink-soft); margin-top: var(--v-3); }
  .product-head { max-width: 62ch; margin-bottom: var(--v-6); }
  .product-head p { color: var(--v-ink-soft); margin-top: var(--v-4); }
  .product-receive { display: grid; gap: var(--v-6); }
  .product-free__handoff { margin-top: var(--v-8); }
  .product-structure__list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: var(--v-2) var(--v-5); }
  .product-structure__list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr; gap: var(--v-3); padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--v-line); }
  .product-structure__list li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .product-structure__list h3 { font-size: 1rem; }
  .product-structure__list p { margin: 2px 0 0; color: var(--v-ink-soft); font-size: var(--vs-small); }
  .product-accountable > div { grid-template-columns: minmax(7rem, 8rem) 1fr; }
  .product-accountable dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--v-ink); font-size: var(--vs-small); }
  .product-evidence { padding: var(--v-2) 0 0; }
  .product-evidence .d-meta { padding: 0 var(--v-5); }
  .product-evidence .d-panel__foot { margin-top: var(--v-2); }
  .product-pro { background: transparent; }
  .product-pro .d-panel__body p { margin: 0; }
</style>
